 "about": "The components the data scripts build, in one place (read by validation/python/registry.py): add_components.py adds a batch's constants, fit_properties.py fits the temperature correlations of every component here, gap_report.py --fetch stores their ThermoML Archive values under the 'thermoml' search names. Fields: coolprop, the CoolProp 8.0.0 fluid name (null: not a CoolProp fluid, so ChemSep); cas, for a component taken from ChemSep; chemsep_file 2, a compound taken from chemsep2.xml (v8.31 data 2) instead of chemsep1.xml; thermoml, the names searched in the ThermoML Archive. The order is the order of the records and reports. Components built from measured data alone (dichloromethane, 2-methoxyethanol) are in measured_components.py.",
